  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM-END-SMOKE-MISSING-READINESS-POLL" ;
  triage:title "run_peer_pair.py starts the daemon then issues commands with no readiness poll" ;
  triage:description "QA-AM-CRITICAL-PHASEEND (important, flaky-test-qa FTQ-004): scripts/smoke/run_peer_pair.py:500's execute() (AI.13 peer-pair smoke / just smoke peer-pair) starts the daemon via subprocess.Popen then runs the preflight/version command and smoke cases immediately with no readiness poll -- the first command can transiently fail on a slow host, unrelated to the feature under test. Sibling scripts (run_admission_capacity.py's await_daemon_ready, run_thorough_shared_host.py) already have the correct poll-with-deadline pattern; this script doesn't follow it. Fix: add the same await_daemon_ready-style helper before issuing any client command." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
